<!--Post: 2708--><!--Time: 1103985983-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2708"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, December 25, 2004 - 6:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If one personality of a multiple commits a crime, the body is held accountable whether the other personalities had knowledge of the crime or not. <BR> <BR>I do believe that BTK&#39;s actions are demonic. He may be oppressed and under demonic influence at times. He is responsible and accountable for his actions, regardless. He can experience a change of heart, but the criminal justice system holds the body accountable for its deeds. <BR> <BR>Anyone with a compulsion driven behavior &#40;drugs, alcohol, shopping, porn, child molestation, puking, incest, etc.&#41; who tries with all their might and white knuckles to change their behavior, knows full well what it is like to be dealing with something that seems to have a life of its own. The person digs and digs trying to get out of the pit they are in, and they just go deeper. It is a lost and isolating and lonely and desparate experience. <BR> <BR>Some doors were meant to be kept closed. If we open one of those doors, we have to live forever with what we find behind that door: The door I opened seemed so small, and now so great, it will not close at all. <BR> <BR>BTK opened a door and a serial killer was born. Often what we think is our freedom of choice turns out to be our prison and undoing. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
