<!--Post: 2710--><!--Time: 1103993422-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2710"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dawgar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dawgar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, December 25, 2004 - 8:50 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Teardrop  <BR>I have to truly say rarely have I ever heard it put as well as you just have!  I agree 110% <BR>It is about choices and opening doors, and if anyone disagrees, just as a heroin or meth addict. <BR>I think at least when he was committing the murders he was possessed or oppressed.  and for those of you who disagree thats ok ...you have your opinion and i have mine...i can neither prove nor you disprove anything...its just a matter of beliefs.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
